     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Paroxysmal AF \"pill-in-the-pocket\":"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " some clinicians provide a single oral flecainide 300 mg (≥70 kg; otherwise 200 mg) or propafenone 600 mg (otherwise 450 mg) self-taken @ onset of palpitations; only w ⍉SA/AV node dysfun, bundle branch block, QT prolongation, Brugada or struct Hdz; an AV nodal blocker (BB or NDHP CCB) lowers the risk of 1:1-conducting flutter."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Slowing the atrial rate can allow 1:1 AV conduction of flutter or a paradoxical rise in ventricular rate in AF; a (−) chronotrope (digoxin or BB) lowers this risk; ⍉recommended for chronic AF."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Dose (PSVT/paroxysmal AF):"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " start 50 mg q12h; raise by 50 mg BID ⍉more often than every four days; max 300 mg/day."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "CI:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " second- or third-degree AV block or bifascicular block w.o a pacemaker, cardiogenic shock; ⍉after recent MI (CAST: excess mortality w class Ic after MI)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Interactions:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " w amiodarone, halve the flecainide dose and check plasma levels; cytochrome P450IID6 inhibitors (ex, quinidine) can raise flecainide levels; w propranolol, both levels rise and (−) inotropy = additive; digoxin levels rise 13–19%."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Correct hypo-/hyperkalemia b4 starting; reduce or stop if the QRS widens; trough plasma level USU 0.2–1 mcg/mL (SE may increase, esp above 1 mcg/mL); levels are required in severe renal or hepatic impairment."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "OD:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ⍉specific antidote; hemodialysis does ⍉remove it."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
